//? Title: K-way merge through actual heap operations
//? Subtitle: Original run identities, duplicate handling and measured tuple-comparator work
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Merging sorted runs must emit every value in global order without repeatedly
searching every remaining element. A minimum-front heap keeps one candidate from
each nonempty run and replaces only the front just consumed. We inspect actual
push/pop identities, retain the original three runs, and distinguish measured
heap comparator calls from the original N log2 K and N(K−1) theoretical curves.
Deduplicating output still consumes every original identity.
)

\toc

> One front per active run

If each run is nondecreasing, its front is its smallest remaining value. The
minimum of all remaining values is therefore the smallest active front. Pop that
front, emit it, and insert the next value from its source run. Induction gives
sorted output containing every original identity exactly once. Empty runs
contribute no front.

Native heap keys are(value,list identity,within-list index), so equal values
preserve original run priority and within-run order. Union merge uses the same
producing heap but discards a popped value equal to the last emitted one. It
does not avoid processing duplicate identities. Input sortedness and combined
output geometry are checked in full before allocation. Integer extremes need no
value arithmetic.

For K supplied rows, N values and R nonempty runs, work is O(K+N log(R+1)), with
O(R) heap and O(N) ordinary output. Complete validation costs O(K+N). Captured
heap operations and comparator counts exclude sorting checks, copies, output
writes, allocation and time.

> Actual equal-valued fronts

Use runs(1,1,4),(1,2) and an empty row. The two equal values from list0 precede
list1’s equal value. The diagram names the first actual popped identity and
actual queue occupancies; the table retains all producing operations, not a
simulated priority queue.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/k_way_merge_fronts.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/merge.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    const auto t = dm::algorithms::k_way_merge_trace({{1, 1, 4}, {1, 2}, {}});
    std::print("| actual ordinal | push or pop | value | original run | original index | heap before | heap " "after | emitted |\n| ---: | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < t.steps.size(); ++i) {
        const auto &e = t.steps[i];
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", i,
                   e.kind == dm::algorithms::MergeHeapKind::Push ? "push"
                   : "pop", e.value, e.list, e.index, e.heap_before,
                   e.heap_after, e.emitted);
    }
    const auto &e =
        *std::find_if(t.steps.begin(), t.steps.end(), [](const auto &e) {
        return e.kind == dm::algorithms::MergeHeapKind::Pop;
    });
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("before", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual fronts before pop\n{}", e.heap_before)).node(
        "value", {6, 0},
        std::format("Actual popped value {}\nrun {}, index {}", e.value, e.list,
                    e.index)).node("after", {12, 0},
                                   std::format("Actual fronts after pop\n{}",
                                               e.heap_after)).edge("before",
                                                                   "value").edge("value", "after").save_svg("build/k_way_merge_fronts.svg");
}
```
