> Measured work beside the original cost models

Keep the original N=3000 and K=2,4,…,64. This time each K performs a real
complete merge: place increasing values0 through2999 into runs by i modulo K,
retaining within-run order. The comparator increments once per actual
whole-tuple heap ordering call. It does not count each integer comparison inside
that tuple operation. Counts depend on the standard-library heap, not a fixed
universal formula.

The original N log2 K heap model and N(K−1) scan-all-fronts model remain
explicitly theoretical reference formulas; neither is relabelled as measured
comparisons or elapsed time. The plot divides all counts by N to make the
definitions directly comparable. Only the native heap trace supplies measured
work.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/k_way_merge_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/merge.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <cmath>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    constexpr std::size_t N = 3000;
    std::vector<double> x, y, h, s;
    std::print("| K | actual values | actual tuple comparisons | heap model N log2 K | scan model N times K " "minus1 |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t k = 2; k <= 64; k += 2) {
        std::vector<std::vector<int>> runs(k);
        for (int i = 0; i < int(N); ++i)
            runs[i % k].push_back(i);
        const auto a = dm::algorithms::k_way_merge_analyze(runs);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {:.6f} | {} |\n", k, a.values.size(),
                   a.work.node_comparisons, N * std::log2(double(k)),
                   N * (k - 1));
        x.push_back(k);
        y.push_back(double(a.work.node_comparisons) / N);
        h.push_back(std::log2(double(k)));
        s.push_back(k - 1);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, y, "actual tuples", {37, 99, 235}, 2).line(x, h, "log2 K model",
                                                         {22, 163, 74}, 2).line(
        x, s, "K-1 model", {220, 38, 38}, 2).y_limits(-2, 72).title(
        "Actual tuple calls beside explicit original models").x_label(
        "number of original runs K").y_label("count or model divided by N").save_svg("build/k_way_merge_work.svg");
}
```
