> Scope and verification

All rows must be nondecreasing, checked in full even for rows that a malformed
caller might expect to ignore. Combined N/output/counter geometry is checked
before allocation. Scalar and count-only calls retain no input/history and no
optional quota. Trace mode owns complete original rows/values, actual heap
operations and output. The million-entry default counts K+N original records
plus actual operations, admitted before copies/heap operations; zero disables
only this optional ceiling. Output/runtime storage, tuple fields, capacities and
bytes/RAM are excluded, so it is not a peak-memory guarantee.

Independent flattened/sorted multiset outputs and a separate ordered heap oracle
checked1000 ordinary/union runs and72016 actual push/pop records, including
source identities, queue occupancies and emission decisions. Another1000 studies
preserved frozen ordinary/union/two-way outputs exactly. Native tests also
retain every original N3000 profile case and cover sortedness rejection, integer
extremes, empty rows, quotas and ownership. The ten-report shared build
passed141 native CTest cases,45 directly instrumented
address/undefined-behaviour sanitizer cases,90 compiled/executed public
examples,412/412 scoped file definitions plus11/11 changed lagged-Fibonacci
engine definitions, and ten representative clangd hovers. All four complete
report programs executed and all four native figures were visually reviewed.
Receipts and repeatable checks are retained under
`build/mepml-conversion/batch-184-193/`.

> References

D. E. Knuth, The Art of Computer Programming, Volume3: Sorting and Searching,
second edition(1998), chapter5,
[author’s book page|https://www-cs-faculty.stanford.edu/~knuth/taocp.html]. The
actual standard-library tuple ordering and explicit selected counters are native
implementation contracts.
